    "ix.12": "⛔ <b>Gate:</b> don’t open the Phase 3 problem until students have finished the surface and deep activities. Meeting the problem too early turns inquiry into guessing.",
    "ix.13": "Big idea & objectives",
    "ix.14": "<b>Big idea:</b> People weigh <b>push and pull factors</b> and real constraints when deciding whether and how to build a new life — and those millions of choices shaped U.S. immigration, industrialization, and cities.",
    "ix.15": "<b>Know:</b> why people immigrated around 1900, what arrival at Ellis Island involved, and how immigration fed industrial cities.",
    "ix.16": "<b>Understand:</b> the same event looks different from each stakeholder’s point of view.",
    "ix.17": "<b>Do:</b> run the problem-solving process end to end — define a problem, gather information, weigh options, choose and defend a solution, and evaluate it (§113.16(c)(26)(B)).",
